只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Scheduled tasks (cron) for DeepSeek Harness: model- and human-callable scheduling that fires followup/inject into agent sessions","id":"gh:1334706363","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-cron","slug":"cofy-x/dsh-cron","topics":["cron","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Scheduled tasks (cron) for DeepSeek Harness: model- and human-callable scheduling that fires followu"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"p/inject into agent sessions"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-cron"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A durable calendar Trigger adapter for DSH Automation. It turns one-shot or recurring schedule occur"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"rences into idempotent fresh-Session Runs. It never executes an Agent turn itself."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Responsibility boundary"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- dsh-cron owns schedule parsing, timezone calculation, durable occurrence identity, catch-up policy"},{"id":"p6s2","text":", and the task-center UI.\n- dsh-automation owns the Run queue, canonical fresh Sessions, cross-worke"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"r concurrency, cancellation, explicit retries, event history, retention, and crash recovery.\n- dsh-w"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"ebhook is the equivalent event-driven Trigger adapter and optionally provides outbound settlement ca"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"s the equivalent event-driven Trigger adapter and optionally provides outbound settlement callbacks."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Requires Node.js 24 or newer, DSH `0.1.5-rc.1` or newer within the `0.1.x` line, and dsh-automation "},{"id":"p8s2","text":" Node.js 24 or newer, DSH `0.1.5-rc.1` or newer within the `0.1.x` line, and dsh-automation `0.2.x`."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Install dsh-automation first, then the adapter:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"To test unreleased source revisions, install from GitHub instead:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The plugin contributes a browser task center through its `dsh.client` manifest and works in headless"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" profiles through tools, commands, and RPC."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Scheduling semantics"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Supported schedules:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- five-field cron: minute, hour, day-of-month, month, day-of-week;\n- one-shot RFC 3339 `at` timestam"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"ps with an explicit offset or `Z`;\n- IANA time zones with daylight-saving-aware occurrence calculati"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"with an explicit offset or `Z`;\n- IANA time zones with daylight-saving-aware occurrence calculation."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"For every calendar occurrence, the scheduler persists a run record and advances the schedule before "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"submitting Automation. The stable identity and key are derived from the job id and scheduled instant"},{"id":"p17s3","text":". If the process dies after Automation commits but before the source store records its Run id, resta"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"rt submits the same key and receives the same Run."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Missed recurring occurrences use an explicit latest-only catch-up policy: the newest due instant run"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"s once, older backlog is not replayed. A one-shot remains as durable history after it fires. Pausing"},{"id":"p18s3","text":" preserves the schedule; resuming advances recurring schedules past the current time."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Each job uses concurrency key `cron:<job-id>` with a configurable limit (currently one by default). "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"dsh-automation enforces the limit transactionally across every worker and process."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Model tools:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"- `cron_add` — create a recurring or one-shot job;\n- `cron_update` — pause or resume;\n- `cron_list` "},{"id":"p22s2","text":"— inspect schedules, occurrences, linked Runs, and outcomes;\n- `cron_remove` — delete a job."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Commands:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Jobs created by a command or model tool capture the creating Session's absolute workspace as a fresh"},{"id":"p25s2","text":" Automation target. Browser/API jobs must send `cwd` or inherit `defaultCwd`. Migrated legacy jobs w"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"ithout either are safely paused with a `migrationIssue` until retargeted."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Durable reconciliation"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Occurrence records progress from `submitting` to the linked Automation state and terminal projection"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ords progress from `submitting` to the linked Automation state and terminal projection. They retain:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- deterministic `occurrenceId`, `scheduledAt`, and `idempotencyKey`;\n- linked `automationRunId` and "},{"id":"p28s2","text":"current Run state;\n- terminal completion time, outcome, result excerpt, or error."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The adapter consumes the durable Automation feed with checkpoint `cron.adapter.v1`. On an expired cu"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"rsor, it refreshes every linked Run by id and resumes at the published prune watermark. Terminal set"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"tlement is emitted only once for optional callback integration."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"The source store keeps bounded terminal history but never trims active occurrence records. Schema v1"},{"id":"p30s2","text":" migrates to v2 on load; old `lastRun` data remains readable as a `legacy` occurrence."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"| Key | Default | Meaning |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| `dataDir` | `$DSH_HOME/cron` | durable job store and "},{"id":"p32s2","text":"scheduler lock directory |\n| `defaultTimeZone` | host zone | zone used when a cron expression omits "},{"id":"p32s3","text":"one |\n| `maxJobs` | `64` | maximum active jobs |\n| `minIntervalMinutes` | `1` | minimum recurring in"},{"id":"p32s4","text":"terval |\n| `defaultCwd` | none | absolute fallback workspace for browser/API jobs |\n| `reconcilePoll"},{"id":"p32s5","text":"Ms` | `1000` | Automation event-feed poll interval |\n| `maxRunHistory` | `100` | retained terminal o"},{"id":"p32s6","text":"ccurrences per job |"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"Only the scheduler-lock holder arms timers, submits pending occurrences, and reconciles the feed. Ot"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"her processes sharing the same Harness home expose management services and can take over after the h"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"s sharing the same Harness home expose management services and can take over after the holder exits."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Management writes use a separate short-lived cross-process lock, collision-free sequence sidecar, an"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"d record-level three-way merge. A process adopts peer additions and untouched edits without resurrec"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"ting deletions; prolonged lock contention fails closed instead of overwriting peer state."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"The adapter requires the public `dsh-automation >=0.2.0-alpha.0 <0.3.0` service contract. It does no"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"t import private dsh-automation source and requires no deepseek-harness modification."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

